-- src:2069 | A State agency shall not be eligible for a performance bonus payment with respect to any fiscal year for which the State agency has a liability amount established under subsection (c)(1)(C).
@ref s 2025(d)(3) prohibition on receipt of performance bonus payments (src:2069)
GIVEN `the State agency has a liability amount established under subsection (c)(1)(C) for the fiscal year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(d)(3) the State agency is eligible for a performance bonus payment for the fiscal year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A State agency shall not be eligible for a performance bonus payment with respect to any fiscal year for which the State agency has a liability amount established under subsection (c)(1)(C)"
        IF `the State agency has a liability amount established under subsection (c)(1)(C) for the fiscal year` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for a fiscal year "for which the State agency has a liability amount established"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2071 | A determination by the Secretary whether, and in what amount, to award a performance bonus payment under this subsection shall not be subject to administrative or judicial review.
@ref s 2025(d)(4) payments not subject to judicial review (src:2071)
GIVEN `the determination is the Secretary's determination whether, and in what amount, to award a performance bonus payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(d)(4) the determination is subject to administrative or judicial review` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be subject to administrative or judicial review"
        IF `the determination is the Secretary's determination whether, and in what amount, to award a performance bonus payment` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "A determination by the Secretary whether, and in what amount, to award a performance bonus payment"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2073 | A State agency may use a performance bonus payment received under this subsection only to carry out the program established under this chapter, including investments in—
-- src:2074 | (A) technology;
-- src:2075 | (B) improvements in administration and distribution; and
-- src:2076 | (C) actions to prevent fraud, waste, and abuse.
@ref s 2025(d)(5)(A)-(C) use of performance bonus payments (src:2073-2076)
GIVEN use IS A `s 2025(d)(5) use of a bonus payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(d)(5) the State agency may use the performance bonus payment for the use` MEANS
    CONSIDER use
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may use a performance bonus payment received under this subsection only to carry out the program established under this chapter"
    WHEN `s 2025(d)(5) a use that does not carry out the program established under this chapter` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2081 | (B) The Secretary shall not award performance bonus payments to State agencies in fiscal year 2019 for fiscal year 2018 performance.
@ref s 2025(d)(6)(B) no bonus payments in fiscal year 2019 for fiscal year 2018 performance (src:2081)
GIVEN `fiscal year of the award` IS A NUMBER
      `fiscal year of the performance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(d)(6)(B) the Secretary may award performance bonus payments` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary shall not award performance bonus payments to State agencies in fiscal year 2019 for fiscal year 2018 performance"
        IF `fiscal year of the award` EQUALS 2019 AND `fiscal year of the performance` EQUALS 2018 THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on awards "in fiscal year 2019 for fiscal year 2018 performance"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2025(e) Use of social security account numbers; access to information`

-- src:2083 | The Secretary and State agencies shall (1) require, as a condition of eligibility for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program, that each household member furnish to the State agency their social security account number (or numbers, if they have more than one number)
@ref s 2025(e)(1) each household member shall furnish a social security account number (src:2083)
GIVEN `the household member has a social security account number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household member has furnished to the State agency every social security account number they have` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(e)(1) the household member has met the condition of eligibility of furnishing a social security account number` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text speaks of the number "or numbers, if they have more than one number" and does not say what follows for a member who has none
        IF (NOT `the household member has a social security account number`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the household member has furnished to the State agency every social security account number they have` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "require, as a condition of eligibility for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program, that each household member furnish to the State agency their social security account number"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2083 | and (2) use such account numbers in the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2025(e)(2) use the numbers in the administration of the program (src:2083)
GIVEN `the Secretary and State agencies use the account numbers in the administration of the program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(e)(2) the account numbers are used in the administration of the program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary and State agencies use the account numbers in the administration of the program` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary and State agencies shall ... (2) use such account numbers in the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2083 | The Secretary and State agencies shall have access to the information regarding individual supplemental nutrition assistance program applicants and participants who receive benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 1381 et seq.] that has been provided to the Commissioner of Social Security, but only to the extent that the Secretary and the Commissioner of Social Security determine necessary for purposes of determining or auditing a household’s eligibility to receive assistance or the amount thereof under the supplemental nutrition assistance program, or verifying information related thereto.
@ref s 2025(e) access to the information provided to the Commissioner of Social Security (src:2083)
GIVEN `the applicant or participant receives benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary and the Commissioner of Social Security determine that access is necessary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is for determining or auditing a household's eligibility or the amount of assistance, or verifying information related thereto` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(e) the Secretary and State agencies shall have access to the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the access is to the information "regarding individual supplemental nutrition assistance program applicants and participants who receive benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act"
        IF (NOT `the applicant or participant receives benefits under title XVI of the Social Security Act`) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but only to the extent that the Secretary and the Commissioner of Social Security determine necessary for purposes of determining or auditing a household's eligibility"
        IF (NOT `it is for determining or auditing a household's eligibility or the amount of assistance, or verifying information related thereto`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the Secretary and the Commissioner of Social Security determine that access is necessary` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the Secretary and the Commissioner of Social Security determine that access is necessary` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the determination of the Secretary and the Commissioner was not supplied
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2025(f) Payment of certain legal fees`

-- src:2085 | Notwithstanding any other provision of law, counsel may be employed and counsel fees, court costs, bail, and other expenses incidental to the defense of officers and employees of the Department of Agriculture may be paid in judicial or administrative proceedings to which such officers and employees have been made parties and that arise directly out of their performance of duties under this chapter.
@ref s 2025(f) counsel fees for officers and employees of the Department of Agriculture (src:2085)
GIVEN `the person defended is an officer or employee of the Department of Agriculture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is judicial or administrative and the officer or employee has been made a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it arises directly out of their performance of duties under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expense is counsel fees, court costs, bail, or another expense incidental to the defense` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(f) the expense may be paid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person defended is an officer or employee of the Department of Agriculture`
            AND `the proceeding is judicial or administrative and the officer or employee has been made a party`
            AND `it arises directly out of their performance of duties under this chapter`
            AND `the expense is counsel fees, court costs, bail, or another expense incidental to the defense`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the payment is of expenses "incidental to the defense of officers and employees of the Department of Agriculture ... in judicial or administrative proceedings to which such officers and employees have been made parties and that arise directly out of their performance of duties under this chapter"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2025(i) Geographical error-prone profiles`

-- "payment error rates (as defined in subsection (d)(1))": subsection (d)(1) does not define the payment error rate; (c)(2)(A) does (NOTES.md, finding 4).
-- src:2326 | (1) The Department of Agriculture may use quality control information made available under this section to determine which project areas have payment error rates (as defined in subsection (d)(1)) that impair the integrity of the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2025(i)(1) quality control information (src:2326)
GIVEN `the information is quality control information made available under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(i)(1) the Department of Agriculture may use the information to determine which project areas have payment error rates that impair the integrity of the program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the information is quality control information made available under this section` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may use quality control information made available under this section"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2327 | (2) The Secretary may require a State agency to carry out new or modified procedures for the certification of households in areas identified under paragraph (1) if the Secretary determines such procedures would improve the integrity of the supplemental nutrition assistance program and be cost effective.
@ref s 2025(i)(2) new or modified procedures for certification (src:2327)
GIVEN `the area was identified under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines the procedures would improve the integrity of the program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines the procedures would be cost effective` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(i)(2) the Secretary may require the State agency to carry out new or modified certification procedures` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in areas identified under paragraph (1)"
        IF (NOT `the area was identified under paragraph (1)`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the Secretary determines the procedures would improve the integrity of the program` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `the Secretary determines the procedures would be cost effective` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Secretary determines such procedures would improve the integrity of the supplemental nutrition assistance program and be cost effective"
        IF `the Secretary determines the procedures would improve the integrity of the program` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            OR `the Secretary determines the procedures would be cost effective` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a determination of the Secretary was not supplied
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2025(j) Training materials regarding certification of farming households`

-- "annually thereafter" is read as each anniversary of the first deadline (fork F-6 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2329 | Not later than 180 days after September 19, 1988, and annually thereafter, the Secretary shall publish instructional materials specifically designed to be used by the State agency to provide intensive training to State agency personnel who undertake the certification of households that include a member who engages in farming.
@ref s 2025(j) 180 days after September 19, 1988, and annually thereafter (src:2329)
GIVEN `years after the first deadline` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 2025(j) the date by which the instructional materials are due` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `years after the first deadline` EQUALS 0 THEN JUST ((Date 19 9 1988) PLUS 180)
        IF `years after the first deadline` GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST (`add years` ((Date 19 9 1988) PLUS 180) `years after the first deadline`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a negative number of years is before the first deadline
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 2025(j) instructional materials published (src:2329)
GIVEN `years after the first deadline` IS A NUMBER
      `date the materials are published` IS A DATE
      `they are specifically designed for the State agency to provide intensive training to State agency personnel who undertake the certification of households that include a member who engages in farming` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(j) the instructional materials are published as required` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2025(j) the date by which the instructional materials are due` `years after the first deadline`
    WHEN JUST due THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `date the materials are published` AT MOST due AND `they are specifically designed for the State agency to provide intensive training to State agency personnel who undertake the certification of households that include a member who engages in farming` THEN JUST TRUE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than 180 days after September 19, 1988, and annually thereafter, the Secretary shall publish instructional materials"
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text gives no deadline for a negative number of years after the first deadline
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
